<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nitta Yoshisada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1301–1338</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nitta Yoshisada was a Japanese warrior of the Minamoto line who joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-go-daigo">Emperor Go-Daigo</a> against the Hojo regents. In 1333 he stormed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamakura">Kamakura</a>, destroying the Kamakura <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a> and opening the Kenmu Restoration. He remained loyal to Go-Daigo when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-takauji">Ashikaga Takauji</a> rebelled, fighting for the Southern Court until he was killed in battle in 1338.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nitta-yoshisada.jpg" alt="Nitta Yoshisada" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nitta_Yoshisada.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
